              "numbering": "21.4",
              "text": "21.4 Except in respect of Excluded Claims, the total aggregate liability of each Party to the other Parties arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall not exceed the greater of (a) the amounts paid or payable by that Party under this Agreement in the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim and (b) one million US dollars (US$1,000,000). For the purposes of this Subparagraph 21.4, \"Excluded Claims\" means a Party's indemnification obligations under Subparagraph 21.2, a Party's breach of Paragraph 31 (Confidentiality), and a Party's gross negligence, wilful misconduct or fraud."
